WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.389 --> 00:00:04.056
(dramatic music and sirens)

00:00:05.317 --> 00:00:07.860
- Boxin', to me, is like
a way of motivation,

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.243
of gettin' out the hood.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.940
Bein' a kid growin' up in Chicago,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.563
you see a lot of drug dealin',
gang-banging shootouts.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.950
But, we're in the city showin' kids, like,

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.760
this isn't just a bubble,

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.631
and this is how everything gives in life.

00:00:24.631 --> 00:00:25.464
(bell dings)

00:00:25.464 --> 00:00:26.850
You gotta have a belief in yourself

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.850
that you can see mo' than this;
you can be better than this.

00:00:30.845 --> 00:00:33.460
(two thuds)

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.870
- [Narrator] This Great Big
Story is made possible by

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.663
"The Chi" on Showtime.

00:00:39.854 --> 00:00:43.187
(ambient street sounds)

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:48.645
(punching bag being hit)

00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:50.330
- Bend your knees a little bit, power.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.540
Remember to use your waist.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:52.640
OK?

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:53.906
One, two.

00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:54.773
Nice.

00:00:54.773 --> 00:00:55.943
Right.

00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:57.982
Nice, remember to turn on that foot.

00:00:57.982 --> 00:00:58.912
Right.

00:00:58.912 --> 00:01:00.408
Good.

00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:01.377
Jab.

00:01:01.377 --> 00:01:03.160
(serious instrumental music)

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:03.993
Jab.

00:01:03.993 --> 00:01:04.826
Better.

00:01:04.826 --> 00:01:05.660
Jab.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.220
My name is Sally Hazelgrove,

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:10.690
and I am the founder and
executive director of

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.460
Restoring the Path: Crushers Club.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.293
Jab.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.640
In 2000, I was livin' in Chicago,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.340
and I started studying gangs
and interviewing gang members,

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.687
and I asked them in 2004,

00:01:24.687 --> 00:01:27.000
"What's something that would
get you off the block?"

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.713
And, "boxing" was their number one answer.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.340
From hearing their stories I
started to formulate a vision.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:37.033
In March of 2013, I opened Crushers Club.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.370
Crushers Club is a place where youth come

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.130
as an alternative to gangs,

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:48.880
and as a way to terminate
off of juvenile probation.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.015
- Take your time.

00:01:50.015 --> 00:01:51.173
It took me a month.

00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:54.245
It took me like two weeks
to a month to get this.

00:01:54.245 --> 00:01:55.625
You learned in one day.

00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:56.532
Good.

00:01:56.532 --> 00:01:57.448
Keep it high.

00:01:57.448 --> 00:01:58.281
- [Sally] Since opening our doors,

00:01:58.281 --> 00:02:00.520
we've seen over 500 youth.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.530
They can let down their guard.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.150
They can be young men.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.180
They can empathize with eachother.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.133
They can be funny.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.890
I tell all of them, "It's your
job to save all the children.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.310
I'm here to empower you,
and for you to lead."

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.123
Because they are the change makers.

00:02:18.047 --> 00:02:19.343
- [Male Coach] Take a turn.

00:02:19.343 --> 00:02:20.176
Good.

00:02:20.176 --> 00:02:21.009
Good.

00:02:22.967 --> 00:02:27.967
(somber instrumental music and sirens)

00:02:28.293 --> 00:02:31.440
- I didn't have no easy
experience bein' in Chicago.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.160
When I was 6, I seen my daddy get shot

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.750
right in front of me.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.070
I had so little close friends to me,

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.290
and friends just in general
that just gettin' killed

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.270
off gun violence.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.603
After while, like for me,
death just became normal.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.780
I started comin' to Crushers
Club when I was 9 years old.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.567
Ever since then, I just been boxin'.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.940
I have to look at the bigger picture,

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.810
instead of just seein' the
streets and bein' enticed by it,

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.093
what you see everyday.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.440
'Cause honestly drug dealers,
boosters, people sellin' weed,

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.220
people sellin' crack, all that stuff,

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.563
it entice you do that, to
be that type of person.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.373
But I know I'm bigger than the street.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.090
The boxin' ring was like almost
my guidance and my therapy.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.850
Anytime I had an issue,
anytime I had a problem,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:26.760
anytime I felt some type of way,

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.630
as soon as I stepped foot in Crushers Club

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:30.943
I felt like I was on top.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:35.737
(somber instrumental music)

00:03:46.561 --> 00:03:48.978
- I ain't know what that was.

00:03:51.984 --> 00:03:54.949
- I want four ya'll run this
way, four ya'll run that way.

00:03:54.949 --> 00:03:56.050
- I'm runnin' this way.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.180
- [Sally] We've had a lot
of success at Crushers Club.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.150
I've seen young men that
were on the street, shooting,

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.357
now come to me and say,

00:04:02.357 --> 00:04:05.197
"I no longer gang bang,
and I've put down my gun."

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.750
These are not hardened criminals,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.670
and we're gonna fight for them

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.923
pretty much til our dying breath.

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:20.010
- [Christopher] You look
at all these pictures

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.130
of all these kids, you not
just thinking about yourself

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:25.360
you thinkin' about the kids.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.470
You is a kid, you can
still have a kid life,

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.350
you can still do the basic things that

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.833
any other kid at any other city wanna do.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.360
You feel that family
environment, that family vibe

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.600
when you in here.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.510
I know what I'm doin',

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.210
I wouldn't be the same person

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.387
if it wasn't for Crushers
Club or for boxin'.

00:04:46.387 --> 00:04:48.280
I feel like this ain't even
like my real beginnin',

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.443
'cause I got way more to go.

00:04:51.368 --> 00:04:53.735
This just like, tip of the iceberg.

00:04:53.735 --> 00:04:56.068
(two thuds)

